  * `P` - Pawn\n        * Color (Player):\n            * `W` - White (moves first)\n            * `B` - Black\n        * 2Step (En Passant flag)\n            * `F` - Did NOT move 2 squares last turn\n            * `T` - Moved 2 squares last turn (en passant eligible)\n        * Moved (Movement flag)\n            * `1` - Has moved before\n            * `0` - Has NOT moved yet\n        \n        ### Examples: \n            * PWF1: White Pawn, not available for en passant, already moved; \n            * RBF0: Black Rook, never moved (castling eligible);\n            * KWT1: White king, irrelevant 2-step flag, has moved;\n            * QWF0 = White queen, irrelevant 2-step flag, never moved.\n\n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output one of the valid actions with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n        ', 'user_prompt': 'You are playing as Black.\nCurrent state representation is as follows:\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n8 |RBF0|    |    |    |KBF0|    |    |RBF0| 8\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n7 |PBF0|PBF0|BWF1|BBF1|BBF1|    |PBF0|PBF0| 7\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n6 |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 6\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n5 |    |    |    |PBF1|QWF1|PBF1|    |    | 5\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n4 |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 4\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n3 |    |    |    |    |    |NWF1|    |    | 3\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n2 |PWF0|PWF0|    |    |PWF0|PWF0|PWF0|PWF0| 2\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n1 |RWF0|    |    |    |KWF0|BWF0|    |RWF0| 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a7-a5, P: a7-a6, R: a8-b8, R: a8-c8, R: a8-d8, P: b7-b5, P: b7-b6, P: d5-d4, B: d7-c6, B: d7-b5, B: d7-a4, B: d7-e6, B: d7-c8, K: e8-f7, K: e8-f8, K: e8-g8, P: f5-f4, P: g7-g5, P: g7-g6, P: h7-h5, P: h7-h6, R: h8-g8, R: h8-f8]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Evaluation:  \nLooking at the current position, Black has several potential moves, but key considerations include:\n\n- The white queen on e5 is dangerously centralized and exerts pressure on key squares, including targeting Black’s king via possible discovered attacks.\n- Black\'s light-squared bishop on d7 is blocked in and could be repositioned to exert pressure (e.g., b5 or c6).\n- The pawn push a7-a5 gains space on the queenside and supports future …b7-b5 ideas, while also potentially opening lines for the a8 rook.\n- The move Bb5 would attack the knight on f3 (Nf3 equivalent here on f3 — currently NWF1 on f3), which is unprotected. However, Bd7-b5 is not immediately safe due to the white pawn on e4? But wait — e4 is empty. White has pawns on e2, f2, etc., but no piece blocking d7-b5. Let\'s verify: from d7 to b5, path is clear, and b5 is empty. So Bxb5 might be good, but Bb5 without capture applies.\n\nWait — valid moves list includes: **B: d7-b5** — this is a non-capture move to b5. That places the bishop on b5, attacking the knight on f3 (NWF1). This knight is undefended, so following up with …Bxf1 or …QxN after Qa5+ or similar could be powerful.\n\nBut wait — can we play …Bb5? Yes, it\'s in the valid moves list. And after Bb5, if White doesn’t respond, …Bxc1 or …